      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks, that's helpful. I'm thinking about the actual diversity of the talent pool we're seeing though. In our experience, some of the most brilliant operational minds we interview have different cultural ways of communicating—maybe they're a bit more reserved, or their style of eye contact or vocal emphasis is different from what you described. \n\nIf we see a candidate who is highly competent but doesn't fit that \"polished\" or \"assertive\" Western mold you mentioned, how should we weigh that? Is there a risk that we're implicitly filtering out great leaders just because they don't match those specific polished markers?",
